(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["ce-easy-2026-004"]={"v":1,"id":"ce-easy-2026-004","title":"Advance Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE","sourceTitle":"Advance Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE","branch":"CIVIL ENGINEERING","code":"CE","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering","seriesId":"ce-easy-2026","num":4,"category":"advance","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering"},"source":"CIVIL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering/004_Advance Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Read the sentence to find out whether there is any grammatical error in it. The error, if any will be in one of the sentence. If there is no error, then answer will be (d).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5a5f35280124c235014a.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nThe alarming report of an earthquake frightened everyone in that disaster prone village.</p>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Select the word that is <strong>NEAREST</strong> in meaning to the bold word in capital letters <strong>VENERATE</strong></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Accuse"},{"key":"B","html":"Reverence"},{"key":"C","html":"Criticize"},{"key":"D","html":"Abuse"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nVenerate means to regard with great respect which is similar in meaning to Reverence meaning<br />\ndeep respect for someone or something.</p>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>There are multiple routes to reach from node A to node B as shown in the network.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/39ae345ee0fa58cf48f9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The cost of travel on an edge between two nodes is given in rupees. Nodes 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 are toll booths. The toll price at toll booths marked 1 and 5 is Rs. 40 and is Rs. 20 for the other toll booths. Which is the cheapest route from node A to node B?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A - 1 - 3 - B"},{"key":"B","html":"A - 2 - B"},{"key":"C","html":"A - 6 - 2 - B"},{"key":"D","html":"A - 6 - 5 - B"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e8/e86f7d1bbfda211af582.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Read the following information carefully and answer the question below it:<br />\nRahul’s roll number in IES exam is a number consisting of three non-zero distinct digits, such that the sum of the digits at hundred’s and unit’s place is equal to that of half of the digit at ten’s place. Also the sum of all the possible three digit numbers obtained using these three digits without repetition is 2664. The digit in the tens place is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"6"},{"key":"B","html":"8"},{"key":"C","html":"9"},{"key":"D","html":"2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2d5def3b00fcdd32c629.png\" /></div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A rectangular water tank is 80 m × 40 m. Water flow into it through a pipe of 40 cm<sup>2</sup> at the opening at a speed of 10 km/h. By how much, the water level will rise in the tank in half an hour?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/73a53911482e0be9380b.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/22360287fde6ed3268aa.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/8058e86614e5ffab1163.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/75/758c594d78cef8a8d216.png\" /></div>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The question given below is followed by three statements. You have to study the question and all the three statements given to decide whether any information provided in the statement(s) is/ are redundant and can be dispensed with while answering the given question.<br />\nWhat is the cost of painting the two adjacent walls of a hall at Rs. 5 per m<sup>2</sup>, which has no windows or doors?<br />\nI. The area of the hall is 24 m<sup>2</sup>.<br />\nII. The breadth, length and height of the hall are in the ratio of 4 : 6 : 5 respectively.<br />\nIII. Area of one wall is 30 m<sup>2</sup>.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"I only"},{"key":"B","html":"II only"},{"key":"C","html":"III only"},{"key":"D","html":"Either I or III"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f23c81803e92c92f03a9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The average income of <em>A</em>, <em>B</em> and <em>C</em> is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f5/f5ae7f0b7b63290e7c50.png\" /> per month and the average income of <em>B</em>, <em>C</em> and <em>D</em> is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e3e3202c20520f3f9c35.png\" /> per month. If the average salary of <em>D</em> is twice that of <em>A</em>, then the average salary of <em>B</em> and<br />\n<em>C</em> is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e2d6fbdd0759b6af3142.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"8000"},{"key":"B","html":"18000"},{"key":"C","html":"13500"},{"key":"D","html":"9000"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/63/63dd4d3b9766433c03bd.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>There are total 100 coins consisting of 20 paise, 50 paise and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/86/8667ab61c5defa02a13f.png\" /> in the ratio of 7 : 8 : 5. What is the number of coins of 50 paise if the difference between the amount yielded by 20 paise and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0ed8643c45a12f9a89f3.png\" /> coin is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5af38904b199a805c628.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"32"},{"key":"B","html":"40"},{"key":"C","html":"26"},{"key":"D","html":"56"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/11/11e67f9e6ac18d50bd4b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The average weight of a class of students is 67.5 kg. The weight of the class teacher is 25% more than the average weight of the class. The average weight of the class is less than the class teacher by <em>x</em>%. The value of <em>x</em> is:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"33.33%"},{"key":"B","html":"25%"},{"key":"C","html":"20%"},{"key":"D","html":"can’t be determined"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/8143b026d0dd8594b96b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In the figure, if it is given that <em>O</em> is the centre of the circle and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/38/38e7b31f897f1d40d406.png\" /> is_____</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/31/31d22736d17a6d306516.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"105°"},{"key":"B","html":"130°"},{"key":"C","html":"150°"},{"key":"D","html":"75°"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/16f5ce759c21d4907c2e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The inner diameter of a 50 mm thick hollow cylinder is 150 mm. The diameter of kern of this hollow cylinder is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"75 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"80 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"85 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"95 mm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c2/c2deb5c4ca03e461ed5f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A concrete beam is pre-stressed with a parabolic tendon is shown in the figure. The eccentricity of the tendon is measured from the centroid of the cross-section. The applied pre-stressing force at service is 1750 kN. The uniformly distributed load of 50 kN/m includes the self-weight.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/33/33ae4e8a91389b5e16b9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The stress at 4 m from left support in the top fibre is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"14.72 MPa (tensile)"},{"key":"B","html":"14.72 MPa (compressive)"},{"key":"C","html":"18.65 MPa (tensile)"},{"key":"D","html":"18.65 MPa (compressive)"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3fa4538df5ad3e572fee.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/0805c671d9f0f9f3dd45.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Member(s) of the truss shown below carries/carry zero force is/are</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6f/6fa58c8f7f9b58d9e4ba.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"EC only"},{"key":"B","html":"EC and AB"},{"key":"C","html":"EC and AC"},{"key":"D","html":"EC, AC and AB"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/682af8f6fa1e67d49920.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Efflorescence in saline soils occurs primarily due to</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Downward percolation of water rich in salts into the groundwater table"},{"key":"B","html":"Absorption of carbon dioxide by the soil surface leading to salt precipitation"},{"key":"C","html":"Upward movement of water from the water table carrying dissolved salts, followed by evaporation at the surface"},{"key":"D","html":"Flow of water from inside the roots into the soil by osmosis"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nDownward percolation of water through the soil containing salts is called leaching. The phenomenon<br />\nof salts coming up in solution and forming a thin crust on the surface after evaporation of water<br />\nis called effloresence.</p>"},{"n":15,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For satisfactory disinfection, a total chlorine dosage of 0.65 mg/l is required at a pH of 7 with required contact time at this pH being 12 minutes. If the same degree of disinfection is to be achieved at a pH of 8, what will be the contact time (in minutes, rounded off to one decimal place)<br />\nrequired? Take coefficient of dilution, n = 1.5; ionisation constant, k<sub>i </sub>= 2.7 × 10<sup>–8</sup> mol/l.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[59.5,60],"answerText":"59.7","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>59.7 (59.5 - 60)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d6df8b18fb2fd6e725a5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b88f5ae0ca9379d50117.png\" /></div>"},{"n":16,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In a fatigue test on bituminous mix, a single point sinusoidal load of 2000 N is applied with 10 Hz frequency to a spacimen of size (100 × 100 × 750) mm<sup>3</sup> as shown in figure. A maximum deflection of 1.5 mm was noted and the specimen was found to sustain 5.3 × 10<sup>7</sup> repetitions till occurence of failure (constant strain). The stiffness modulus of the bituminous mix is _______ MPa. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9a/9a4879676882dcffc1fb.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1405,1407.5],"answerText":"1406.81","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1406.81 (1405 - 1407.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/aa/aa1e6fa6b12fbb0e0d0a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following instrument(s) is/are used to determine horizontal distances?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Geodimeter"},{"key":"B","html":"Tellurometer"},{"key":"C","html":"Mekenometer"},{"key":"D","html":"Distomat"}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c, d)</p>"},{"n":18,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A hauched (varying depth) reinforced concrete beam is simply supported at both ends, as shown in the figure. The beam is subjected to a uniformly distributed factored load of intensity 12 kN/ m. The design shear force (expressed in kN) at the section X-X of the beam is _______. (Neglect variation of load due to change in section).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9d9628e5345d77d0456a.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[22.6,23],"answerText":"22.8","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>22.8 (22.6 - 23.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/93/93666ff3386dd16ecf55.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":19,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A solid circular shaft made from an elasto plastic material has stress-strain diagram as shown in figure. The radius of the shaft is 40 mm. The maximum torque that can be applied if the angle of twist is not to exceed 0.6 radian in 3 m length will be _________ (in kNm, correct upto two<br />\ndecimal places).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cb55adf4ca08f5e1e2a9.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[18.7,19.05],"answerText":"18.88","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>18.88 (18.70 - 19.05)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/35596f3e4a11a43774c7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8c/8c45be22a4e4e364b718.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A proposed open well is to be constructed in a formation consisting of coarse sand. The required discharge from the well is 0.005 m<sup>3</sup>/s, operated under a depression had of 3 m. The specific yield of the formation for coarse sand may be taken as 1.1 m<sup>3</sup>/hr/m<sup>2</sup> per meter of depression head. Assuming steady pumping conditions, the required diameter of the open well is _____ m. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.62,2.66],"answerText":"2.64","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.64 (2.62 - 2.66)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4b/4bb651766f9a7c92fe32.png\" /></div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Let the probability density function of a random variable <em>X</em> be given as:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/06/06dc666e4a744b0e8f62.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>where <em>u</em>(<em>x</em>) is the unit step function. Then the value of <em>b</em> and probability <em>p</em> {<em>x</em> ≤ 0} respectively, are</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e4/e47877b8f2aefe8731bf.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/80292dd173d9c36b09ad.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1a/1a71761fb0f2201a6145.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/38/3872a2505cf7839641a2.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/57/5762f7a6f256e3e50509.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Let u(x, t) satisfy the initial and boundary value problem <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91ad145a06753b4a79ab.png\" /> u(0, t) = u(π, t) = 0, t > 0 and u(x, 0) = sin(x) + 2sin(4x), 0 < x < π, then the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5fb0008f829c00d4864e.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d1/d11213d6057b65acaf41.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d67611d159bc6dea390d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e95d7a04558281c13930.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/98caf3f2b7d163cd084c.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9f330f9123b40d685be.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Based on Meyerhof’s bearing capacity theory which of the following statement(s) are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"It is a general theory of bearing capacity for a strip footing at any depth"},{"key":"B","html":"Failure mechanism is similar to that assumed by Terzaghi, but with extended failure surface above foundation level."},{"key":"C","html":"Shear strength of soil above the footing base was not accounted in the analysis."},{"key":"D","html":"Meyerhof’s theory can be used for footing on slopes."}],"answer":["A","B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0c/0cc688dd1a241bc653e7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In an open channel, the flow area is related to the depth of flow by the expression A = y<sup>2.7</sup>, where y is in meters. If the critical depth of flow in the channel is 0.6 m, then the specific energy corresponding to this critical state is _________ m. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.68,0.74],"answerText":"0.71","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.71 (0.68 - 0.74)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/147090ec0d920981fdd9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A 15 mm thick gusset plate is connected to 12 mm thick flange plate of an I-section using fillet welds of size 10 mm on both sides as shown in figure (not drawn to scale). The gusset plate is subjected to a point load of 300 kN acting at a distance of 120 mm from the flange plate.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/76/7636db5b6e18b2680df2.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The maximum resultant stress (equivalent stress) in the fillet weld in vertical plane would be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"92.15 MPa"},{"key":"B","html":"95.25 MPa"},{"key":"C","html":"112.28 MPa"},{"key":"D","html":"115.82 MPa"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/5381735cbf551412721b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":26,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A clay layer of 6 m thickness is overlain by a sand layer of 2 m thickness and underlain by rock, as shown in figure. The saturated unit weight of sand is 21 kN/m<sup>3</sup> and that of clay is 19.0 kN/m<sup>3</sup>. The ground water table lies at top of sand layer. It is estimated that the additional stress on clay<br />\nlayer due to weight of building is 150 kN/m<sup>2</sup> at top of clay layer and 70 kN/m<sup>2</sup> at bottom of clay layer due to construction of building. The compressibility behaviour of clay is described by following relationship between applied stress and void ratio:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5adaa9e67cc3ce0150d5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/736d1777335cdf33a40b.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"90 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"108 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"120 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"125 mm"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a7/a76cf1412642f7f70199.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/6541f67242d5f544fd0b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A city has a population of 220000. The fire demand for this city using Freeman’s formula for fire demand is _____ cumecs. (Answer upto three decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.015,1.03],"answerText":"1.022","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.022 (1.015 - 1.030)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e4/e407cdba2c7f01e63cf1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":28,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A 6 hour unit hydrograph is to be converted into a 12 hour unit hydrograph. According to the superimposition method, which of the following steps is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Add the ordinates of the 6 hr UH to the ordinates of another identical 6 hr UH logged by 12 hours, then divide all ordinates by 2"},{"key":"B","html":"Add the ordinates of the 6 hr UH to the ordinates of another identical 6 hr UH without any lag, then multiply all ordinates by 2."},{"key":"C","html":"Add the ordinates of the 6 hr UH to the ordinates of another identical 6 hr UH lagged by 6 hours, then divide all ordinates by 2."},{"key":"D","html":"Divide all ordinates of the 6 hr UH directly by 2 to get the 12 hr UH"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":29,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The natural frequency in side sway for the frame shown in figure below is _______ rad/sec<br />\n(Round off to nearest integer) Take: EI = 24 × 10<sup>12</sup> Nmm<sup>2</sup> and g = 10 m/sec<sup>2</sup>.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e2c2c63cd20c08550ba1.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[20,20],"answerText":"20","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>20 (20 - 20)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/01208a47859e1f664588.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In a boundary layer subjected to an adverse pressure gradient, which of the following correctly<br />\nindicates the condition exactly at the separation point?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Wall shear stress negative, velocity profile forward"},{"key":"B","html":"Wall shear stress is zero, beginning of flow reversal"},{"key":"C","html":"Wall shear stress is maximum,velocity profile uniform"},{"key":"D","html":"Wall shear stress zero; velocity gradient positive"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nAt the separation point, the shear stress is zero and the velocity gradient is 0.</p>"},{"n":31,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A layer of clay 6 m thick lies between two layers of sand, upper sand layer extends from ground level to a depth of 4 m and water table being 2 m below the ground level. Lower sand layer is under artesian pressure, the piezometric level being 5 m above ground, the saturated unit weight<br />\nof clay and sand are both 20 kN/m<sup>3</sup>, and coefficient of volume compressibility for clay is 9.0 × 10<sup>–4</sup> m<sup>2</sup>/kN. Due to pumping from the artesian layer the piezometric level falls by 3 m. The consolidation settlement of the clay layer is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"68.67 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"83.05 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"79.46 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"47.50 mm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f189c134bc50604629d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A single-stage bio-filter is to treat 5 million litres per day of sewage having a raw BOD concentration of 330 mg/l. The primary clarifier removes 30% of the raw BOD, and the treated effluent from the bio-filter must have a BOD not exceeding 60 mg/l. The filter has an organic loading rate of 0.8 kg/day/m<sup>3</sup>. The recirculation ratio for this filter is:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0.247"},{"key":"B","html":"0.593"},{"key":"C","html":"0.343"},{"key":"D","html":"0.420"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a5/a535acd888a6d735695d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following statement(s) about the physical property of aggregates used in bituminous macadam construction are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Los Angeles abrasion value is tested as per IS : 2386 (Part IV) and its maximum value is 40%."},{"key":"B","html":"Aggregate stripping value is tested as per IS 6241 and its maximum value is 25%"},{"key":"C","html":"Water absorption is tested as per IS : 2386 (Part III) and its maximum value is 5%"},{"key":"D","html":"Soundness test (loss with sodium sulphate test) is done as per IS : 3286 (Part V) and its maximum value is 12%."}],"answer":["A","B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)<br />\nWater absorption maximum value is 2%.</p>"},{"n":34,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The hypotensual allowance for a chain length of 20 m is found to be 0.15 m. The gradient of the ground can be expressed as 1 in _______ (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8.12,8.17],"answerText":"8.15","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>8.15 (8.12 - 8.17)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0d6483b8897125956534.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A vector field <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c7/c78e7c4de93f562bcc7a.png\" /> The value of line integral <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b4c58c2a751d4f9d9448.png\" /> where <em>C</em> is the circular path given by x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/39174c9b4b5bca255430.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/be/befcf6fe7da2387d3265.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e5042fae29039a0bc732.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0ebe71b4db2020fdf7fe.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/eb/eb80189b8cfc3d38d5ea.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>According to the disinfection behaviour of chlorine, which of following statements is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The presence of ammonia results in formation of chloramines hence increasing the efficiency of disinfection."},{"key":"B","html":"Free available chlorine takes 100 times more time than combined available chlorine for the same dosage."},{"key":"C","html":"Hypochlorous acid is formed in greater quantities at low pH hence decreasing the pH increases the effectiveness of chlorine."},{"key":"D","html":"Increase in the temperature of water results in decrease in the killing power of both free and combined chlorine."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":37,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A homogeneous square plate of side <em>L</em> = 1 meter and mass m = 2 kg is suspended from the mid point of one of the sides as shown in figure. The frequency of vibration of plate is _________ (in rad/sec, correct upto two decimal places).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4f/4f36ff268465e0c3a4c7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.4,3.46],"answerText":"3.43","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.43 (3.40 - 3.46)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d4/d40b014c94220ac5fc00.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Compaction of an embankment is carried out in 600 mm thick layer, the rammer used for compaction has a foot area of 0.06 m2 and energy imparted in every drop of rammer is 500 N-m, assuming 40% more energy in each pass over the compacted area due to overlap. The number of passes required to develop compaction energy equivalent to the Indian Standard light compaction is _______. (Answer in integer).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[30,32],"answerText":"31","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>31 (30 - 32)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1e/1e922db467b35245f3ec.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which of the following is a incorrect property of silica fume as puzzolanic material in concrete?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Exhibits latent hydraulic action in the presence of calcium hydroxide"},{"key":"B","html":"Has comparatively low heat of hydration, making it suitable for mass concrete"},{"key":"C","html":"Increases the tendency of bleeding in concrete"},{"key":"D","html":"Reduces the porosity and thus permeability too"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":40,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Dry unit weight of coarse sand is 16 kN/m<sup>3</sup>. For mechanical stabilization, 5.5 kN of mixture of dry sand and silt is added to 1 m<sup>3</sup> of coarse sand and the total volume of soil mass increased by 20%. The specific gravity of all soil solids are 2.67 and assume all soils are dry initially. The<br />\nreduction in the porosity of the soil is ________ (Correct upto three decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.07,0.076],"answerText":"0.073","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.073 (0.070 - 0.076)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a880d492f561704d5880.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A trapezoidal channel has a bottom width of 4 m and side slopes 1 H : 1.5V. If the critical depth of flow in the channel is observed to be 1.80 m, then the discharge corresponding to this condition is _______ m<sup>3</sup>/s. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[35.2,35.7],"answerText":"35.45","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>35.45 (35.20 - 35.70)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/9244811cfe45e095a015.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":42,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A main canal, which off-takes from a storage reservoir, is used to irrigate crops in a region having three agricultural seasons in a year. The data of crops grown and their duties at the head of the main canal are tabulated below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec8567d7a519da7bd18c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>If the time factor for the main canal is 0.65, then the discharge required at the head of the main canal is ______ cumecs. (Answer upto two decimal places, neglect losses from canal head to field).</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[7.4,8],"answerText":"7.69","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>7.69 (7.40 - 8.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2a/2a6f718c314a35534ea0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A river flowing at 27 m<sup>3</sup>/s with an initial dissolved oxygen of 9.3 mg/l mixes with 3 m<sup>3</sup>/s of wastewater whose 5-day BOD is 220 mg/l. The 5-day BOD of river is 4 mg/l. The deoxygenation and re-aeration constants respectively are 0.1 day<sup>–1</sup> (base 10) and 0.3 day<sup>–1</sup>(base 10). If the saturation dissolved oxygen of river is 9.3 mg/l, then the dissolved oxygen of the mixture after 2 days is _______ mg/l. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.9,2],"answerText":"1.96","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.96 (1.9 - 2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/41/4140555f1413830e92f5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For a gradually varied flow profile, consider the behaviour of the water surface elevation gradient <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/41/412b5057daa347ead5e9.png\" /> at key depths. Which of the following statements is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/82a67d8a24c7d1ca4b69.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fe/feb6f4c9298fb215b0d8.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a1a1cbcce1bbe7878a2c.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/63/63fa35c9b35a0c80d9ec.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fa5690305a308a4e744c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>For the rigid jointed frame as shown in figure, the horizontal displacement of the roller support due to applied load of 25 kN will be (Assume members are axially rigid). Take, flexural rigidity of all members as 1 × 10<sup>6</sup> kNm<sup>2</sup>.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99c4b4ae09c20bf5217e.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.54 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"1.2 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"0.85 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"0.93 mm"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5e0d585b7f3c1234a46.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":46,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A ground level source emits 1600 g/day of SO<sub>2</sub> into an untable atmosphere. At a downward distance of 1100 m, the dispersion coefficients are:<br />\n• Crosswind direction, σ<sub>y</sub> = 156<br />\n• Vertical direction, σ<sub>z</sub> = 110.2<br />\nThe mean wind speed is 5 m/s. The ground-level concentration of SO<sub>2</sub> at a downward distance of<br />\n1100 m (at the plume centreline) from the source is ________ μg/m<sup>3</sup>. (Answer upto three decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.06,0.08],"answerText":"0.069","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.069 (0.060 - 0.080)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/25/2577f30f96fecfeee895.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Let <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/9f/9fe9469a59a3bb5397bb.png\" /> then the value of 2<em>A</em> + 3<em>B</em> + <em>C</em> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3"},{"key":"B","html":"4"},{"key":"C","html":"5"},{"key":"D","html":"6"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1dd15a9b6d0cc5477b37.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":48,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The number of linearly independent eigen vectors of the matrix <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/40e76d55d0f98ffc44c7.png\" /> is _____.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3,3],"answerText":"3","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3 (3 - 3)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c8dd9f16765809ebc5f2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A dual wheel assembly carrying 2000 kg on each bar trails a pavement of thickness 200 mm. Centre to centre spacing between the two tyres is 280 mm and clear gap between the wall of the tyres is 100 mm. The value of ESWL of given assembly is ___________ kg. (Answer to nearest integer value).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2975,2980],"answerText":"2977","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2977 (2975 - 2980)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d589066521b14a19fdab.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/443583ccc26213db05cf.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A tank contains three immiscible fluids with specific gravities as:<br />\nAir (negligible density); Oil (S = 0.7), Water (S = 1); Mercury (S = 13.6). A gauge connected at point A shows a reading of – 17.2 kPa.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8a/8ab929e774ccf5070dab.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The level difference of mercury level (x) in the U-tube column due to this gauge reading is _____ m. (Answer upto three decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.595,0.615],"answerText":"0.605","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.605 (0.595 - 0.615)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c3/c35f5be01245c57a367a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A circular water tank carrying a total load of 300 tonne is supported on a ring wall having outer diameter 6.0 m and inner diameter 5.0 m. The vertical stress at a depth of 8 m located at the centre of circular area is ________ tonne/m<sup>2</sup>. (Correct upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.64,1.74],"answerText":"1.69","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.69 (1.64 - 1.74)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b2632a8fd72ce64f235e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77b47ec21fd6bafd175c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In a pair of overlapping vertical photographs, the measured parallax difference between the images of the top and bottom of a building is 24 mm. The average flying height above datum at which the photographs were taken is 3200 m. If the elevation of the base of the building is 240 m and the mean distance between the principal points in two photograph is 112 mm, then the height of the building is ________ m. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[489.55,489.75],"answerText":"489.66","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>489.66 (489.55 - 489.75)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/42d482e4d83e09c8cddb.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A normally consolidated clay sample has a liquid limit of 70% and plastic limit of 30%. According to Alpan’s (1967) correlation, the value of the coefficient of earth pressure at rest, k<sub>0 </sub>of the soil is ______. (Correct upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.54,0.58],"answerText":"0.56","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.56 (0.54 - 0.58)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d1/d15bfc005dbbefdf08a0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A swampy area prevents direct chaining between points P and Q, so the surveyor runs two lines around the obstruction as shown in the figure (not drawn to scale).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1cc82dba5995ba70e499.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>From the figure, determine the distance <em>PQ</em>.</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"934.68 m"},{"key":"B","html":"987.74 m"},{"key":"C","html":"959.54 m"},{"key":"D","html":"918.27 m"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c6473a47e6e7e5aac8c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":55,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>An ISA 75 × 75 × 6 mm is connected to a 12 mm gusset plate using five M18 bolts of grade 4.6 as shown in figure below. The block shear strength of the plate is:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/1951c7e829bdf50dd4b9.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"207.94 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"242.09 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"165.25 kN"},{"key":"D","html":"274.96 kN"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/62/6206af09819245b892a7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A water treatment plant treats 20000 m<sup>3</sup>/day of water. The total chlorine applied is 12 kg/day.<br />\nAfter the required contact period, the measured residual chlorine in the treated water is 0.3 mg/<em>l</em>. The chlorine demand of the water is _______ mg/<em>l</em>. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.3,0.3],"answerText":"0.30","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.30 (0.30 - 0.30)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/80fb64e7b1bc089331ab.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For a two dimensional flow field, the velocity components are given by,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c0/c050610b2b814ece0d18.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following statements is correct for this flow?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The flow is compressible and rotational"},{"key":"B","html":"The flow is incompressible but rotational"},{"key":"C","html":"The flow is compressible but irrotational"},{"key":"D","html":"The flow is incompressible and irrotational"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/781278a98f7a589b4937.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":58,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Triaxial test done on a pavement using the following data: wheel load = 5000 kg, radius of contact area = 16 cm, traffic coefficient, X = 1.5, rainfall coefficient, Y = 0.9, design deflection, Δ = 0.25 cm, E-value of subgrade soil, <em>E<sub>s</sub></em> = 100 kg/cm<sup>2</sup>, E-value of base course material E<sub>b</sub> = 400 kg/cm<sup>2</sup>, E-value of 8.5 cm thick bituminous concrete surface course = 1000 kg/cm<sup>2</sup>. Then the required base course thickness is:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"59.50 cm"},{"key":"B","html":"69.04 cm"},{"key":"C","html":"77.23 cm"},{"key":"D","html":"75.45 cm"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/31/313cbde533e6382f30b5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For a certain catchment, the S-hydrograph corresponding to a rainfall of 1 cm/hr is described by the relation:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/82eb1e9b205d0b586c18.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>where t is in hours. Using this information, a 2 hours unit hydrograph is to be developed. The runoff ordinate of this 2 hour unit hydrograph at 3-hours from the start is ______ m<sup>3</sup>/s. (Answer upto two decimal places).</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.25,0.29],"answerText":"0.27","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.27 (0.25 - 0.29)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bccbbac0f2d07147458b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The number of trains and their corresponding speeds on a curved board gauge section with 440 m radius are given in table below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a1a4fed1f4ddb0688d48.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If the gauge (centre to centre distance between the rail heads) is taken as 1750 mm, then the required equilibrium cant will be</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"8.2 cm"},{"key":"B","html":"8.8 cm"},{"key":"C","html":"9.2 cm"},{"key":"D","html":"9.5 cm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/75/75216c8a08a14f3b6f2d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":61,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A project has six activities as shown in the table. If the fixed cost is Rs. 300 per day, then optimum duration of project after crashing is _______ days. (Answer to nearest integer)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/43/437fb499ebd43fa6e409.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[14,14],"answerText":"14","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>14 (14 - 14)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/84/84daa7680b318dfb0c9e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A beam is built in at B and propped at A as shown in figure. The support at B has loose fit that allow the beam to rotate though an angle of 0.5° in counterclockwise direction.<br />\nTake <em>E</em> = 72 GPa, <em>I</em> = 120 × 10<sup>6</sup> mm<sup>4</sup></p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7e/7e92d1f476af5121306a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following option(s) is/are correct ?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Vertical reaction at propped end is 58.38 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"Vertical reaction at propped end is 51.63 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"Moment at <em>B</em> is 33.48 kNm"},{"key":"D","html":"Moment at <em>B</em> is 38.45 kNm"}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8b/8badb9f57e2b1dfb6b9b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":63,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A random variable X has the following probability function:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c0/c092f372b63f45873904.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The probability <em>P</em>(0 < <em>X</em> < 6) is _____. (Correct upto three decimal places</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.81,0.82],"answerText":"0.816","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.816 (0.810 - 0.820)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/af/afb7da4e144048b8c469.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A function f(x) is differentiated twice such that its differential equation is:<br />\nf (x) – 2f ′(x) + f′′(x) = 0. If f(0) = 1, f ′(0) = 2, then f(x) at x = 1 will be_____. [Correct upto 3 decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5,6],"answerText":"5.436","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5.436 (5.000 - 6.000)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0fe3df5e6ad495aa4add.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The Newton Raphson iteration formula for finding inverse square root of <em>N</em> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/58/583c48591fbecfdd841e.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f9/f9e8a098872a9654bc2d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/33/337ec09c4f5d19dc01ff.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/03/03c660e6adb87de328a5.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/182dc32813d0da06fbb4.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":34,"NAT":27,"MSQ":4},"withoutKey":0}};
